{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-009", "score": 0.102, "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-009 | Study family SF-TMP-009: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- observed_research_question: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The PULL_UP-specific decline with exposure is defensive adaptation rather than shooter selection/lineup artifact.\n- observed_result: With lineup FE: slope holding shot fixed -0.0255 (0.0061); shooter's earlier scored -0.1044 vs not scored +0.0693. No lineup FE: -0.0063 (0.0036); placebo other play types -0.0075 (0.0017).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Effect shrinks from -0.0255 to -0.0063 without lineup FE and the same-shooter placebo on other play types is -0.0071/-0.0075, consistent with shooter-level confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-041", "score": 0.096, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-041 | Study family SF-APPS-041: PUTBACK suppression matched-pair isolation (star vs team)\n- observed_research_question: PUTBACK suppression matched-pair isolation (star vs team)\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: Conceding a PUTBACK causally suppresses the next offensive possession after matching on game state.\n- observed_result: TEAM ATT=-0.0038 CI[-0.025,+0.015] perm p=0.890 n_t=15614. STAR ATT=+0.0040 [-0.049,+0.052] p=0.834 n_t=2481. STAR Q4 ATT=-0.1045 [-0.217,+0.010] p=0.032 (gradient does not survive matching as a FINDING).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- observed_failure_evidence: Raw putback suppression collapses once margin/state is matched; original finding was a score/context confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n_treated team=15614, star=2481\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF30"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-067", "score": 0.095, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-067 | Study family SF-APPS-067: Opponent action T -> your offense T+1 (def-matched 8x8)\n- observed_research_question: Opponent action T -> your offense T+1 (def-matched 8x8)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: The opponent's previous play type changes your next-possession PPP after matching on defensive team.\n- observed_result: 3/64 FINDING cells survive both matchings: SPOT_UP->TRANSITION ATT=-0.085; POST_UP->TRANSITION -0.083; PNR->DRIVE -0.058 (all also survive +prev_made). PULL_UP->DRIVE dropped as defense-quality confound.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Three cells replicate under def-match, off-match, and prev_made control. Most of 64 are null.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 64 cells tested; 3 FINDING\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPS-067: 'matching primary; sensitivity match on own offense. bh-fdr+placebo+ft-clean. prev_made control. 3/64 finding cells survive bot'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-060"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088", "score": 0.09, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-088 | Study family SF-APPS-088: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others\n- observed_research_question: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence.\n- observed_result: Unmatched conn vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08. Usage-matched vs role: paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09 n=96. Vs terminal: +0.0777 t=2.37 p=0.0261 n=25.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Usage-matched connector vs role occupant identity break is large and significant (n=96). Licensed comparison excludes organizers.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=96 matched pairs vs role; n=25 vs terminal; 908 player-seasons\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-014"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
